# The pipeline, the gates and the build inputs: changing any of these needs a build admin's approval of
# the pull request's latest commit, unless a build admin opened it (GOVERNANCE.md, "Roles"). The rulesets
# do not require a code owner's review, since an author cannot approve their own pull request; the
# Gate · Pipeline owner check (.github/scripts/Test-PipelineOwner.ps1) reads this file instead.
# Maintainers and committers can propose such a change; a build admin approves it. The gate reads this
# file from the base branch, so a pull request cannot loosen it for itself. Patterns are plain paths: a
# wildcard fails the gate rather than being guessed at.
# Every pattern must match a file (.github/scripts/tests/CodeOwners.Tests.ps1).

/.github/                   @whizbang-lib/build-admins
/scripts/                   @whizbang-lib/build-admins
/.config/                   @whizbang-lib/build-admins
/Directory.Build.props      @whizbang-lib/build-admins
/Directory.Build.targets    @whizbang-lib/build-admins
/Directory.Packages.props   @whizbang-lib/build-admins
/global.json                @whizbang-lib/build-admins
/nuget.config               @whizbang-lib/build-admins
/dotnet-tools.json          @whizbang-lib/build-admins
/GitVersion.yml             @whizbang-lib/build-admins
/codecov.yml                @whizbang-lib/build-admins
/codecoverage.config        @whizbang-lib/build-admins
/codecoverage.runsettings   @whizbang-lib/build-admins
/sonar.config               @whizbang-lib/build-admins
/BannedSymbols.txt          @whizbang-lib/build-admins
/BannedSymbols.Generators.txt @whizbang-lib/build-admins
